&gt;&gt; You say you need
a lot of samples.

00:16:46.181 --> 00:16:47.010
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:16:47.011 --> 00:16:48.350
&gt;&gt; To compute that.

00:16:48.351 --> 00:16:49.080
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:16:49.081 --> 00:16:51.280
&gt;&gt; Suppose theoretically,

00:16:51.281 --> 00:16:53.160
your sample is
close to infinite.

00:16:53.161 --> 00:16:53.720
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:16:53.721 --> 00:16:54.840
&gt;&gt; Which means that
your minimum is

00:16:54.841 --> 00:16:56.160
actually very, very, very small.

00:16:56.161 --> 00:16:56.920
&gt;&gt; Yes. Yes.

00:16:56.921 --> 00:16:59.995
&gt;&gt; That means that
the more samples that you take,

00:16:59.996 --> 00:17:03.070
the more to the left,

00:17:03.071 --> 00:17:07.375
the redcoats is
going to be like.

00:17:07.376 --> 00:17:07.791
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:17:07.791 --> 00:17:09.930
&gt;&gt; I am talking
